<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 10px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Language Is an Important Skill – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 5px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> My Multilingual Self</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> Language Is an Important Skill</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Speaking: Productive: Describe the process of adapting to a new environment. Interactive: Facilitate peer feedback sessions on presentations.</p>
            <b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Speaking: Can describe personal experiences of adapting to a bilingual environment (e.g., "When I started volunteering at the Biomuseo, learning key English phrases helped me communicate better with tourists and coworkers.")</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can facilitate peer feedback on a classmate's presentation about multilingualism by asking questions and providing constructive comments (e.g., "I think your explanation of the benefits of multilingualism was clear. Maybe you could add an example to make it even stronger.")</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can summarize a peer's strengths during a feedback session (e.g., "You did a great job explaining the challenges of learning a second language, and I liked how you used examples from your personal experience.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
        <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of various countries or communities with different languages. Students are asked: "Imagine you have to move to one of these places. What language challenges do you think you'd face? What language skills would be most important for daily <b>communication</b>? Share your thoughts with a partner." (2 minutes)</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models a response using target vocabulary and grammar: "I believe that adapting to a new country requires high language <b>proficiency</b>. My friend said, 'You <b>can</b> definitely <b>enhance</b> your social life if you <b>learn</b> a few key phrases.' Companies <b>will prioritize</b> hiring individuals with high language <b>fluency</b> for <b>international opportunities</b>." The teacher explicitly uses reported speech and future simple, highlighting /s/ and /z/ sounds in words like "success" and "citizens" and word stress in "multilingualism." (2 minutes)</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms like "proficiency" and "prioritize."</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ 1: "If someone has 'language <b>proficiency</b>,' does it mean they are just starting to learn a language, or are they very good at it?" (Expected answer: Very good.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">CCQ 2: "If a company '<b>prioritizes</b>' something, does it mean it's the least important or the most important to them?" (Expected answer: Most important.)</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher offers examples like: "A business <b>will prioritize</b> customer service over profit in the long run." (2 minutes)</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">7 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Multilingual Self".</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short audio interview excerpt (2 minutes) from a podcast titled "Global Citizens: Adapting Through Languages." The interview features a Panamanian student discussing her experience studying abroad and the role of <b>multilingualism</b> in her personal and <b>career opportunities</b>. The register is informal-academic, focusing on personal anecdotes.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students interact orally to understand the main points of an authentic audio input related to language adaptation and <b>multilingualism</b>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher plays the audio excerpt twice.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question (Speaking):</b> "What was the main challenge the student mentioned about adapting to a new country, and how did her <b>language skill</b> help her overcome it?" (Students discuss in pairs for 1 minute, then one or two pairs share their summary.)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Speaking):</b> Teacher provides two statements for students to discuss if they are true or false based on the audio, justifying their answers. Example: "The student <b>said that multilingualism</b> only offers personal benefits, not professional ones." (Students discuss and justify, using reported speech).</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Practice using reported speech (e.g., "She <b>said that multilingualism</b> opens..."), future simple for predictions (e.g., "Companies <b>will prioritize</b> hiring..."), and modals of ability (e.g., "You <b>can</b>..."). Integration of vocabulary: <b>multilingualism, language, proficiency, communication, career, opportunities, business, education, fluency, skill, said, argued, believe, prioritize, offer, communicate, become, excel, enhance, learn, bilingual, multilingual, proficient, effective, international, diverse, multicultural, necessary, fluent</b>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion & Read Aloud):</b> Teacher provides sentence stems on the board. Students complete them orally in pairs, then read them aloud. Focus on reported speech and future simple. (4 minutes)
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"My friend <b>said that</b> learning a new <b>language</b>..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I <b>believe</b> that <b>multilingualism will</b>..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Our teacher <b>argued that</b> students who <b>excel</b> in languages..."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In the future, global <b>business will prioritize</b>..."</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-Controlled (Structured Q&A):</b> Students work in groups of three. Student A asks a question about language learning/<b>multilingualism</b> (e.g., "What <b>skill can</b> help you in an <b>international career</b>?"), Student B answers using a modal of ability (e.g., "You <b>can become proficient</b> in a language by practicing daily."), and Student C reports Student B's answer using reported speech (e.g., "He/She <b>said that</b> you <b>can become proficient</b> by practicing daily."). Teacher reminds students to pay attention to /s/ and /z/ sounds and word stress. (5 minutes)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction (Discussion Prompts):</b> Teacher gives pairs discussion prompts on cards. Each pair picks a card and discusses for 1-2 minutes, ensuring both students speak and use the target grammar and vocabulary. (3 minutes)
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 1: "How <b>can multilingualism enhance career opportunities</b> in Panama?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Prompt 2: "What advice <b>will</b> you <b>offer</b> someone who wants to <b>become fluent</b> in English for better <b>communication</b>?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">12 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Multilingual Self."</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> "Multilingual Adaptation Experience & Peer Feedback Session." Students will work in groups of three. Each student prepares a short (1-minute) personal narrative or imagined experience about adapting to a new <b>multicultural</b> environment or situation where different <b>languages</b> were necessary. They must use at least two target grammatical structures and four vocabulary words.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Students individually prepare their 1-minute narrative focusing on: "When I started volunteering at the Biomuseo, learning key English phrases helped me <b>communicate better</b> with tourists and coworkers." or "I <b>believe</b> that future <b>opportunities will</b> prioritize those with <b>multilingual proficiency</b>." (3 minutes)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. In groups of three, each student takes turns presenting their narrative. (3 minutes)</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. After each presentation, the other two students facilitate a peer feedback session. They must use the following pragmatic functions and sociolinguistic considerations:
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ask a clarifying question (e.g., "You <b>said that</b> you felt challenged; <b>can</b> you explain more about that?").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Provide constructive feedback (e.g., "I think your explanation of the benefits of <b>multilingualism</b> was clear. Maybe you <b>could</b> add an example to make it even stronger.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Summarize a strength (e.g., "You did a great job explaining the challenges of learning a second <b>language</b>, and I liked how you used examples from your personal experience.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Offer practical, culturally sensitive advice (e.g., "Remember, not everyone has the same <b>education opportunities</b> to learn <b>diverse languages</b>. Be supportive and empathetic when discussing this topic.").</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher circulates, observing and providing discrete support, encouraging natural <b>communication</b> and emphasizing pronunciation of words with /s/ and /z/ sounds and multisyllabic word stress.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">10 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on speaking output and peer feedback facilitation. Additionally, students will complete a quick peer assessment using a simple rubric.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' participation in the "Multilingual Adaptation Experience & Peer Feedback Session" (Stage 4).</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist & Peer Rubric):</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of words, including /s/ and /z/ sounds and correct word stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "multilingualism," "multicultural").</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> (e.g., <b>proficiency, opportunities, communication, skill, fluent</b>).</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target grammar:</b> Reported speech, future simple, modals of ability.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and coherence:</b> Ideas are easy to follow; descriptions are detailed.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration and interaction:</b> Actively listens and provides relevant, constructive feedback using pragmatic functions.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on an index card before leaving:</p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What was one new vocabulary word or grammar point you used confidently today when speaking?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "What is one aspect of your speaking or feedback skills you want to <b>enhance</b>?"</li>
            </ul>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8 min</td>
    </tr>

    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "How did practicing peer feedback today help you better understand the importance of clear <b>communication</b> and respecting diverse language learning backgrounds?"</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "In what future situations <b>will</b> you be able to apply the discussion skills (e.g., giving constructive criticism, summarizing strengths) we practiced today?"</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What worked well in this lesson? The structured peer feedback allowed students to actively use the target language for both describing experiences and providing constructive comments. The focus on specific grammar and vocabulary during practice led to more accurate production. Students engaged well with the scenario "My Multilingual Self." The pronunciation practice was integrated effectively.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? Some students still struggle with fluent use of reported speech in spontaneous conversation; they need more opportunities for repeated, low-stakes practice. For the next lesson (Writing), I need to provide more sentence starters and model paragraph structures that incorporate the same vocabulary and grammar, ensuring a smooth transition from spoken descriptions to written compositions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing Composition), students <b>will</b> build on their speaking practice by writing a paragraph describing a personal or imagined experience of adapting to a new linguistic environment, incorporating feedback mechanisms and the vocabulary and grammar practiced today.</p>
        </td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; vertical-align: top;">8 min</td>
    </tr>
</table>